<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani cotton rates steady in dull trade.</title>
<headline>Pakistani cotton rates steady in dull trade.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton rates held steady on Tuesday in dull trade before a three-day holiday starting Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said the market was likely to open at similar levels on Saturday on low demand from spinners and exporters.</p>
<p>In the kerb market, the NIAB-78 variety was traded at 2,230 rupees ($55.44) per maund (37.32 kg), dealer said.  </p>
<p>Tuesday's official spot rates issued by the Karachi Cotton Association in rupees per maund:</p>
<p>					   Tuesday	    Previous</p>
<p>    NIAB-78 (1996/97 crop)	 2,377.50	   2,377.50</p>
<p>    K-68    (1996/97 crop)	 2,570.00	   2,570.00</p>
<p>    MNH-93  (1996/97 crop)	 2,580.00	   2,580.00</p>
<p>    ($1 = 40.22 rupees)    -- Ovais Subhani 0921-5685192</p>
</text>
